<section id="install" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Install in four steps</h2>
  <ol class="steps-grid">
    <li>
      <h3>Plug in.</h3>
      <p>The T-Echo or the T-Echo Plus into a computer, over USB-C.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Open.</h3>
      <p>Press <span class="mono">RST</span> twice within half a second. A <span class="mono">TECHOBOOT</span> drive shows up.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Drop.</h3>
      <p>The <span class="mono">.uf2</span> file of the <a href="https://github.com/fcatuhe/skyblip/releases">latest release</a> on that drive. The device restarts on skyBlip.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Set up.</h3>
      <p>The aircraft type and your callsign, in the menu under the radar.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="signature">
    The same file works on both devices. After that, updates go through the
    browser, over Bluetooth:
    <%= link_to_page "manage", label: "Manage my skyBlip" %>. For now, only
    development builds are published.
  </p>
</section>

