<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Your questions, answered</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Why the BME280 barometer?</summary>
      <p>It is required for skyBlip conformity. Some T-Echo units are sold without it: pick the version that lists it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need to open or solder the device?</summary>
      <p>No. The device comes assembled. The firmware installs over the USB cable.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do updates cost anything?</summary>
      <p>No. The firmware and its updates are free, and will stay free.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I update from an iPhone?</summary>
      <p>
        No: the update page needs Web Bluetooth, which Safari does not have.
        Use Chrome or Edge, on a computer or on Android. Installing over a USB
        cable, from a computer, needs no browser.
      </p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I go back to Meshtastic?</summary>
      <p>
        Yes. The skyBlip firmware leaves the factory bootloader alone:
        Meshtastic installs again the same way, through the
        <span class="mono">TECHOBOOT</span> drive.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="cta-pair">
